---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { SITE } from '../lib/site'
const updated = '31 May 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — The Reel Vault"
  description="How The Reel Vault handles your data: local-only storage, third-party embeds, and advertising cookies."
>
  <div class="section-head">
    <div><span class="kicker">Your privacy</span><h2>Privacy Policy</h2></div>
  </div>
  <p class="type" style="margin-top:-6px">Last updated: {updated}</p>

  <article class="prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <p>
      This policy explains what information {SITE.name} ("we", "us") collects when you use
      this website, and how it is used. In short: we run no accounts and no database of our
      own, almost everything stays in your browser, and the only data sent off your device
      goes to the third parties whose content and services we embed, described below.
    </p>

    <h3>Information stored on your device</h3>
    <p>
      The Reel Vault keeps your <strong>favourites</strong>, your <strong>viewing
      history</strong> and your <strong>watch progress</strong> in your browser's
      <code>localStorage</code>. This information never leaves your device and is never
      transmitted to us — we have no server that could receive it. You can erase it at any
      time by clearing your browser's site data, or by using the in-app controls (for
      example, "Clear history").
    </p>

    <h3>Information we collect directly</h3>
    <p>
      None. We do not require registration, we do not ask for personal information, and we
      do not operate our own analytics or tracking on the server side.
    </p>

    <h3>Third-party services</h3>
    <p>We rely on the following third parties, each with its own privacy policy:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Internet Archive</strong> — films are streamed and images are loaded
        directly from archive.org. Your browser contacts their servers to play video, and
        they may log requests as described in their own privacy policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Wikipedia / Wikimedia Foundation</strong> — film background information is
        requested from Wikipedia's public API when you open a title's page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Fonts</strong> — typefaces are loaded from Google's font CDN.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Because video and images load directly from these services, those providers can see
      your IP address and standard request information. We do not control and are not
      responsible for their data practices.
    </p>

    <h3>Advertising</h3>
    <p>
      We may display advertising through <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. When advertising
      is enabled, Google and its partners may use cookies — including the
      <strong>DoubleClick / DART cookie</strong> — to serve ads based on your visits to this
      and other websites. Third-party vendors and ad networks may also use cookies, web
      beacons or similar technologies for the same purpose.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting Google's
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
          >Ads Settings</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        You can opt out of many third-party vendors' cookies via
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
          >aboutads.info/choices</a
        > or
        <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
          >youronlinechoices.eu</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        More information is available in
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
          >Google's advertising policies</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Your rights (GDPR / CCPA)</h3>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal
      data, or to object to certain processing. Because we hold no personal data ourselves,
      most such requests should be directed to the third parties above. For anything within
      our control, contact us at
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. Visitors in the EEA,
      UK and California: advertising cookies are used only as described above, and you may
      decline personalised ads using the opt-out links provided.
    </p>

    <h3>Children</h3>
    <p>
      This site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect any
      information from them.
    </p>

    <h3>Changes</h3>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected in the
      "last updated" date above.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:24px">
      Questions about this policy? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
